GIVEN claim  IS A `A Part 2 claim`
      policy IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground under Part 2`
`Part 2 exclusions 1 to 17 that apply to` claim `under` policy MEANS
    `those that hold among`
        (LIST PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 1: intentional or negligent act, with foreseeable consequences`
                   (    (`it was` `an intentional act of the Insured or a Family member` OR `it was` `a negligent act of the Insured or a Family member`)
                    AND `it was` `the consequences were reasonably foreseeable from the act`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 2: liability assumed by agreement`
                   (    `it was` `liability assumed by agreement that would not otherwise attach`
                    AND NOT `the tenant's liability Extension covers the agreement in` claim `under` policy)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 3: injury to a Family member or a person usually residing with the Insured`
                   (`bodily injury` AND `the person injured is Family or usually resides with the Insured` claim)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 4: injury to an employee in the course of work`
                   (    `bodily injury`
                    AND CONSIDER claim's `the person injured`
                        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                        WHEN JUST p  THEN p's `employed by the Insured or a resident and injured in that work`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 5: workers' compensation` (`it was` `a workers' compensation law, judgment, agreement or scheme`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 6: property owned or controlled by the Insured, Family, residents or employees`
                   (    `the property damaged is the Insured's, the Family's, a resident's or an employee's` claim
                    AND NOT `the tenant's liability Extension applies to` claim `under` policy)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 7: business, trade or profession` (`it was` `business, trade or profession of the Insured, Family or a resident`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 8: construction, alteration or repair` (`it was` `construction, alteration, repair or decoration of the Home`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 9: aircraft, vessels, vehicles or internet communication`
                   (   `it was` `aircraft or aerial device (other than a model or toy kite) or airfield`
                    OR `it was` `motor boat or vessel, jetty or mooring`
                    OR `it was` `a road-licensed or compulsorily insured vehicle, or its loading`
                    OR `it was` `email, advertising or internet communication`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 10: communicable disease` (`it was` `transmission of a communicable disease`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 11: use other than as a private residence` (`it was` `use of an Insured Location or land other than as a private residence`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 12: the cost of the Insured's own work` (`it was` `the cost of performing, completing, correcting or improving work`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 13: products no longer in the Insured's control`
                   (    `it was` `goods made, sold or supplied by the Insured and no longer in its control`
                    AND NOT (`it was` `food or drink poisoning at the Insured Location` AND `bodily injury`))
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 13 proviso: every possible precaution with food and drink not taken`
                   (    `it was` `food or drink poisoning at the Insured Location`
                    AND NOT `it was` `the Insured took every possible precaution with food and drink`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 14: professional advice or services` (`it was` `giving or failing to give professional advice or service`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 15: pollution or contamination` (`it was` `pollution or contamination`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 16: fines, penalties or liquidated damages` (`it was` `fines, penalties or liquidated damages`)
            , PAIR `Part 2 exclusion 17: punitive, exemplary or multiplied damages` (`it was` `punitive, exemplary or multiplied damages`))
    WHERE
        `it was` c MEANS elem c (claim's `the circumstances`)
        `bodily injury` MEANS
               elem `death` (claim's `the harm`)
            OR elem `bodily injury, illness or disability` (claim's `the harm`)
            OR elem `fright, shock, mental anguish or nervous injury` (claim's `the harm`)

-- Exclusion 3's two classes. Family membership follows F-family (homecare-definitions.l4).
@ref Part 2, exclusion 3, src:538-547 (fork F-excl3)
GIVEN claim IS A `A Part 2 claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person injured is Family or usually resides with the Insured` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the person injured`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST p  THEN
            `a member of the Family` p
        OR  "usually residing, if the person" ...
                (    p's `has used the Home as a place to live`
                 OR  (    p's `lives with the Insured`
                      AND p's `days the person intends or intended to make the Home the main residence` AT LEAST 60)
                 OR  p's `consecutive days the person used the Home or lived with the Insured` GREATER THAN 90)
    WHERE
        `a member of the Family` p MEANS
            CONSIDER p's `relation to the Insured`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST r  THEN `a relative is in the Insured's Family, being` r `, living with the Insured` (p's `regularly lives with the Insured at the Insured Location`)

-- F-excl3, the literal reading not taken: anyone who "has used the Home" usually resides
-- with the Insured.
@ref F-excl3, literal reading, not taken
GIVEN p IS A `A person injured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`on its literal words, exclusion 3 treats as usually residing` p MEANS
    p's `has used the Home`

@ref Part 2, exclusion 6, src:553-557
GIVEN claim IS A `A Part 2 claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property damaged is the Insured's, the Family's, a resident's or an employee's` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the property damaged`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d  THEN    d's `owned or controlled by the Insured, the Family or a resident`
                      OR d's `belonging to an employee of the Insured`

§§ `Extension: tenant's liability`

-- Tenant's liability, limit 160,000,000 dong for each Occurrence. The exclusion of property
-- in the care and control of the Insured or a servant (exclusion 6) does not apply to loss of
-- or damage to the Insured Location in the Summary, including its fixtures, rented or leased
-- by the Insured; provided it does not apply to liability the Insured assumed by agreement
-- that would not otherwise have attached (other than the tenancy agreement, whose details must
-- be sent to the Insurer when available). It does not apply if the Home is insured under
-- Part 1. F-tenant: where it applies, liability under the tenancy agreement is not excluded by
-- exclusion 2 either, since the Extension names that agreement as the one it reaches.
